wever, if you look at SteamDB today, the game is only kept alive by a handful of people on weekends, which really hurts playability across all multiplayer sections.\n\nThat said, The Anacrusis isn't completely unplayable. You can play the campaign in a private lobby with bots; it has 5 episodes and takes about 2 hours to beat. Honestly, it would have been better if the game had more campaigns, as I suspect that is exactly why so many people walked away from it.\n\nI'm glad I got to play the game, but I'm also disappointed because it could have been something more.", "timestamp_created": 1772350638, "timestamp_updated": 1772350638, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 10, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.538437962532043457", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1642097723", "hardware": {"system_ram": "15977", "os": "Windows 11", "cpu_name": "AMD Ryzen 5 7500F 6-Core Processor             ", "adapter_description": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060", "vram_size": 8187}, "reactions": []}]}